{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"def:geometric-progression","verdict":"matched","note":"{y | ∃ n:ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ y = q^n} is the same set as G_q = {q^n : n∈ℕ, n≥1} for every q, so it holds in particular for q∈(0,1). Leaving the q∈(0,1) domain off the def does not change the set where the paper defines it."}],"assumption_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"ass:independent-tests-default-atom","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"ξ : NondefaultEdge M d → Bool encodes one atom of F_x = σ(S_e(J_{b_e}(x)) : e=(P,i), i<M). Each S_e is a table of independent fair bits and each nondefault edge has its own table, so atoms are exactly the Bool assignments on nondefault edges. chooseChild picks the first i<M-1 whose bit is true and otherwise the default child M-1, so the default is chosen iff all M-1 bits are 0. This matches the core's no-default probability (1-2^{1-M})^d. walkVertices with fuel d starting at the root visits the whole route, and firstDefault returns the first internal vertex on it that picks the default. So isSome ⇔ 'the first default vertex U exists on ξ', both directions. The unused q, g, r0, x binders are harmless because ξ already holds the values addressed at x."},{"obj_id":"ass:conditional-scales-parameters","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"This is the conjunction 0<p<1, M≥2, d≥1, g≥1, r0≥1. The core symbols give exactly these spaces: M ∈ {2,3,…}, d ∈ {1,2,…}, g ∈ {1,2,…}, r_0 ∈ {1,2,…}. That is the paper's 'Fix p∈(0,1) and the construction parameters M,d,g,r_0', in both directions."},{"obj_id":"ass:conditional-scales-default-atom","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"The body is the same as IndependentTestsDefaultAtom: (firstDefault …).isSome. This holds iff some internal vertex on x's route, as determined by the F_x-atom ξ, chooses the default child, i.e. iff 'the route of x uses a default edge'. Equivalent in both directions, with the same atom encoding as above."},{"obj_id":"ass:conditional-scales-height","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"firstDefault … = some U picks out the first internal vertex where the route defaults, which is the paper's U. vertexHeight U = d − depth(U), which lies in {1,…,d} for an internal U, matching the core's 'height h∈{1,…,d}'. Hence 'the first default occurs at U of height h' ⇔ the conjunction, both directions."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

